ded\n  when: cni == \'none\' and (inventory_hostname == groups[\'servers\'][0] or rke2_active_server)\n\n- name: Wait for remaining nodes to be ready - with CNI\n  ansible.builtin.command:\n    cmd: kubectl get nodes --no-headers | grep -c \'Ready\'\n  register: wait_with_cni_result\n  retries: 30\n  delay: 10\n  until: wait_with_cni_result.stdout | int == groups[\'nodes\'] | length\n  when: cni != \'none\' and (inventory_hostname == groups[\'servers\'][0] or rke2_active_server)\n```\n\nThis playbook adheres to the provided task descriptions and is structured for inclusion in an Ansible Role under the `tasks/` directory. The tasks are ordered and named as specified, with the appropriate conditions and configurations applied.' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'phi4:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-21T21:18:16.757467637Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 12480140220, 'load_duration': 2471568689, 'prompt_eval_count': 803, 'prompt_eval_duration': 477618633, 'eval_count': 773, 'eval_duration': 9529725544, 'model_name': 'phi4:14b'} id='run--797dc45a-7b34-41b7-a7c5-5b9610054f2e-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 803, 'output_tokens': 773, 'total_tokens': 1576}
